      "text": [
        " : قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ اَلرَّجُلُ يُوصِي مَنْ يَذْبَحُ عَنْهُ وَ يُلْقِي هُوَ شَعْرَهُ بِمَكَّةَ فَقَالَ «لَيْسَ لَهُ أَنْ يُلْقِيَ شَعْرَهُ إِلاَّ بِمِنًى »."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3090 - Ibn Muskan narrated from Abu Basir, who said: I said to Abu Abdullah (as): \"A man instructs someone to slaughter on his behalf while he discards his hair in Mecca.\"\nImam (as) replied: \"He is not permitted to discard his hair except in Mina.\""
        ]
      }
